## 1. What you may do

Anyone, including companies, may for free:

- download, install, build and run this software;
- test, evaluate and validate it, for example in a proof of concept, a pilot or a test
  environment, and against your own data contracts and pipelines, for up to 90 days per
  organization (the "evaluation period");
- read and study the source code;
- change configuration (environment variables, settings, compose and Helm values) to run it
  for those purposes;
- use it for personal, educational, academic or research purposes that are not commercial;
- share unmodified copies for the purposes above, as long as this license and the copyright notice
  go with them.

## 2. What you may not do without a commercial license

- modify the source code, or distribute modified copies or derivative works;
- use the software in production, or to run any part of a business or its operations;
- sell, rent or license the software, or a product or service that includes it;
- offer the software, or its functionality, to others as a hosted or managed service;
- use it in any other way intended for commercial advantage or monetary compensation.

Testing and evaluating the software during the evaluation period to decide whether to buy a
commercial license is always allowed, even inside a company. "Production" means any use on real
business data or processes that people or systems rely on, or any use after the evaluation period
ends. Personal, educational and research use that is not commercial has no time limit.

